    {
      "id": "r20261117-a02",
      "title": "The Rise of Electric Buses",
      "level": "Menengah",
      "min": 3,
      "body": [
        "For decades, city buses have run on diesel fuel. They are noisy and fill the streets with smoke. Now, many cities are replacing them with electric buses, and passengers are noticing the difference.",
        "Electric buses are much quieter and produce no exhaust. This matters in crowded cities, where dirty air causes health problems. The buses are also cheaper to run: electricity costs less than diesel, and electric motors need fewer repairs.",
        "There are still problems to solve. Electric buses cost more to buy, and cities must build charging stations. On long routes, a bus may need to charge during the day. Even so, experts believe most city buses will be electric within twenty years."
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "decades": "dekade",
        "fuel": "bahan bakar",
        "smoke": "asap",
        "exhaust": "gas buang",
        "crowded": "padat",
        "repairs": "perbaikan",
        "charging stations": "stasiun pengisian daya",
        "routes": "rute"
      },
